# Executor questions

## Summary
Executor `needs_input` output persists a specific question, recommendation and affected requirement on the current issue attempt. The main OpenCode adapter publishes it and requests a correlated human response outside the executor slot and deadline. Independent issues continue integrating.

## Key behavior
- Waiting issues and descendants are blocked. Clarification resumes the same attempt, owned worktree and base commit with a fresh dispatch identity and current approved context. Question history is retained.
- Only active executor time reduces the remaining agent deadline. Human waiting has no timer or attempt charge.
- Answers require adapter-supplied human provenance, the main session, current request/job/attempt/operation/epoch and artifact revisions. Superseded, duplicate and unrelated-session responses cannot advance work.
- An explicit user-correlated `revise_scope` answer carries complete PRD text, graph and issue files. Actual content comparison determines whether approval is needed; graph validation precedes publication. Draft publication records intent and retains old artifacts, approval and integrated-work evidence.
- The normal combined approval gate presents affected and already-integrated issue IDs. Only renewed approval rebinds the unchanged validated baseline. Affected integrated work retains its evidence and is scheduled for execution again; the questioning issue continues the same attempt. Other pending questions receive new revision-bound request identities.
- Public host methods `answerExecutorQuestion` and `continuePlanning` support later responses and approval continuation. Adapter-delivered answers continue automatically. There is no browser write endpoint.

## Code references
- `src/execution/questions.ts` — question persistence, delivery, correlation, scope drafts and approval continuation.
- `src/execution/execute-issue.ts`, `src/execution/attempts.ts` — same-attempt dispatch and remaining active-time budget.
- `src/agents/results.ts`, `src/opencode/adapter.ts`, `skills/tdd/SKILL.md` — structured question output contract.
- `src/planning/approvals.ts`, `src/planning/issues.ts` — revision-bound approval and affected-work presentation.
- `src/execution/scheduler.ts`, `src/core/orchestrator.ts`, `src/commands/router.ts` — independent scheduling and public host boundary.
- `tests/integration/09-questions.test.ts`, `tests/helpers/diamond.ts` — concurrent question demonstration, rejection and renewed approval coverage.

## Related
- [Concurrent execution](concurrent-execution.md)
- [Planning approval](feature-planning.md)

## Notes
The production adapter still reports unsupported human provenance. Tests supply authenticated/correlated user responses through the controllable adapter and real temporary Git repositories; live human-chat and native Linux/Windows runs are not claimed. A prose clarification does not authorize artifact edits; scope revisions use the explicit artifact proposal and normal human approval gate.

